# Unit constructor with @[as-type: fn  guarding: bool] annotation.
# This is the exact pattern used by every leaf TypeNode constructor in prelude.llt:
#   [Leaf@[as-type: [fn [let t] t]  guarding: true]]
# etc.
#
# The @[...] annotation on a unit constructor embeds those key-value pairs in
# FnAnnotation.extra via build_constructor_return_ann (T-1052) + T-1049.
# annotation-of on the resulting Value::Annotated returns the annotation dict directly.
#
# Tests that both `as-type` and `guarding` keys are present with correct values.
# Uses `guarding: true` (same as TypeNode.Int, TypeNode.Float, etc.) and an
# identity function for `as-type` (same as all built-in TypeNode constructors).
[MyNode: [type [Leaf@[as-type: [fn [let t] t]  guarding: true]]]]
[ann: [annotation-of MyNode.Leaf]]
[has-as-type: [has? "as-type" ann]]
[guarding-val: [get "guarding" ann]]
[result: [and has-as-type guarding-val]]
=== out
Dict({"result": Bool(true)})
